## ShipPlaces -- where every part sits on each hull painting, placed by
## hand so guns sit on decks and hardpoints, the reactor in the heart of
## the hull, the warp drive over the stern ahead of the engines, booster
## pods on the aft flanks, and nothing hangs over empty space, an engine
## plume or the middle of a cargo tank.
##
## Points are fractions of the painting (x from the stern edge, y from the
## top).  Keyed "<empire folder>/<file>", or "<folder>/<file>@<hull>" for a
## painting another hull borrows.
##  "w": weapon sockets in hardpoint order (see ShipArt.MOUNTS for the order
##   per hull).
##  "reactor", "qdrv", "sensor", "cloak" (the jammer spine, drawn lying
##   along the hull), "repair", "regen": one spot each.
##  "boost" (booster pods) and "ext" (PDC turrets and shield emitters): the
##   sockets in the order they fill.  A point off the centre line stands
##   for a mirrored pair (its twin at 1 - y, listed right after it); a
##   point on the centre line, or [x, y, 0], is a single socket.  Four numbers
##   are an explicit pair for a lopsided hull.  The order matches the sockets the
##   game made before (ext: mid flanks, bow, fore flanks, aft flanks,
##   stern; boost: beside the engines, then further out), so the socket
##   picks stored in saved designs still land in the same place.
## tools/mount_gallery.gd draws every hull with everything fitted.
class_name ShipPlaces
extends RefCounted

